This implementation uses dynamic programming to efficiently find the optimal 
grouping of books. The key improvements are:



1. Uses a 5-dimensional DP table to store the minimum cost for each combination 
of book counts

2. Considers all possible groupings (5, 4, 3, 2 books) for each state

3. Builds up the solution from smaller subproblems to larger ones

4. Avoids the brute-force nested loops that were causing timeouts



The algorithm will now handle all test cases efficiently while still finding the
optimal discount grouping.

