2. Handles the special case of 'A' correctly

3. Builds the diamond by constructing each line with proper spacing

4. Ensures symmetry by placing characters at mirrored positions

5. Joins all lines with newlines

6. Returns the complete diamond pattern



The diamond is constructed by:

- First building the top half (including the middle line)

- Then building the bottom half (excluding the middle line to avoid duplication)

- Each line is properly padded with spaces to maintain the diamond shape

- The characters are placed at symmetric positions in each line

