I see the issue now. The tests are calling a function named `rows()` but our 
implementation has a function named `get_diamond()`. We need to rename our 
function to match what the tests expect. Here are the corrected files:



diamond.h

```diff
@@ -2,8 +2,8 @@
 
 #include <string>
 
 namespace diamond {
 
-std::string get_diamond(char letter);
+std::string rows(char letter);
 
 }  // namespace diamond
```



diamond.cpp

```diff
@@ -2,11 +2,11 @@
 #include <vector>
 #include <algorithm>
 
 namespace diamond {
 
-std::string get_diamond(char letter) {
+std::string rows(char letter) {
     if (letter < 'A' || letter > 'Z') {
         return "";
     }
 
     std::vector<std::string> diamond;
```



The only change I made was renaming the function from `get_diamond()` to 
`rows()` in both files to match what the tests are expecting. The implementation
logic remains exactly the same, as it was correct - we just needed to match the 
function name that the tests are calling.

